-- title:
--   Finiteness of chart ring modulo a monic polynomial in the modular unit
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, together with the hypothesis that every unit $u$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ whose image under reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial already lies in $H$. Assume also that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$, namely $q^{-1}$ times the integral power series `jNum`, lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios of integral forms for $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, that is, an integral model at $p$ of the curve of level `ΓM M H` over $R_p = \mathbb{Z}$ localised at $p$, carrying properness, flatness, finite presentation, integrality and normality of the structure morphism, a proper smooth model at the auxiliary level, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the geometric base change together with Galois equivariance and a pinning of the chart ring on $q$-expansions, and smoothness and geometric integrality of the generic fibre (the clauses are summarised here). Let $v$ be an element of the finite chart ring `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj`, the $R_p$-subalgebra of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` of elements integral over $R_p[\,j\,]$, and assume that the Laurent series of $v$ is either `modularUnitSeries p`, the quotient $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^p)$, or $p^{12}$ times its inverse. Then there is a natural number $K$ such that for every monic $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ whose constant coefficient is not divisible by $p$, the quotient of `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj` by the ideal generated by $g(v)$ is a finite $R_p$-module, of `Module.finrank` over $R_p$ at most $K \cdot \deg g$. The numerical bound is thus on the rank of the quotient as an $R_p$-module, not on its length.
--
--   This is the finiteness clause for level sets of Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(\tau)/\Delta(p\tau)$ on the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_H(M)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$: cutting the chart ring by a monic integral polynomial in the unit leaves a ring finite over the base. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_finite_etale_quotient_span_aeval_chartAlgFin), where the finite quotients are refined to étale ones.
